  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Are there many people who can speak foreign languages in your country?",
      "speaker": "a",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.73
    },
    {
      "text": "Of course, there are a lot of people who can speak foreign languages in China. But from my perspective, in my social circle, I don't actually know a person who can speak two languages fluently. From the internet, though, I know a lot of people who speak many languages — English, of course, Mandarin and Cantonese, Spanish, Japanese, Korean, and so on. And China is a huge country with a huge population. If you just mean \"speak,\" then yes — even I can say a few Japanese words, like Konnichiwa. Because we have this compulsory education system where every student learns English at school, so everybody can speak some English — maybe not fluently, but they can speak. So I think yes.",
      "speaker": "b",
      "start": 3.18,
      "end": 41.25
    }
  ],
